The updated commit preserves the existing shared Fast contract: on selects `priority`, off or inactive auto clears the override, and no shared control uses the configured baseline. The optional Ultrafast upgrade is applied afterward only when the actual selected native model advertises support in the authenticated catalog. Disabled or unsupported models therefore retain ordinary tier selection. Conflicts with current main are resolved, and fresh independent review found no actionable issues.

Commit: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/commit/f19af83cbba39b9561e8c9e6d48a6877baa0ddb1

@clawsweeper re-review

The final revision adds warm-turn regressions for a previously accepted Ultrafast override followed by Fast off, inactive auto, or unsupported model support, plus configured retry baselines. The earlier Fast-off fixture now follows current main when no tier is inherited: it omits the override. Production behavior is unchanged from the reviewed correction; fresh independent review of the complete candidate found no actionable issues.

